  "title": "WiFi-JEPA: A Self-Supervised Framework for CSI-Based 3D Human Pose Estimation",
  "summary": "WiFi-JEPA introduces a self-supervised learning approach for WiFi-CSI 3D human pose estimation, addressing the limitations of existing WiFi-based systems by leveraging CSI-native representations and a scalable pre-training pipeline. The framework bridges the heterogeneity gap in wireless sensing by decoupling sensing semantics from hardware constraints.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "WiFi-JEPA uses CSI-specific tokenization and link masking to capture 3D spatial structure across heterogeneous signal formats.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The framework employs a ray-tracing simulation pipeline to generate unlabeled CSI data for pre-training, achieving state-of-the-art results on Person-in-WiFi-3D tasks.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "WiFi-JEPA outperforms prior WiFi-CSI baselines in both single- and multi-person 3D pose estimation under the same evaluation protocol.",
      "confidence": 0.95
